{"title":"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution  2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Root\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Root\">roots</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/c/23c2dd73734af39c54bdbad0fb6aa24a98089685.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3+3x^2+4x-11=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"182\" height=\"16\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and that the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/f/0dfc1219725f4689ff8dcf0baf1625820f18c38d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3+rx^2+sx+t=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"169\" height=\"16\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9bbeb7caa1770d1d3cb842655f27e245b08188f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/9/e39beca2e1fc21b28ca4636692562608677fe0f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/3dfbWzOfJAI?t=2785\">https://youtu.be/3dfbWzOfJAI?t=2785</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vieta%27s_formulas\" title=\"Vieta&#39;s formulas\">Vieta's formulas</a> on the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49ee75e14a1d56931e688b77104ff4c1ec117214.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x) = x^3+3x^2+4x-11 = (x-a)(x-b)(x-c) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"434\" height=\"19\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d9bd01ecfbf9beab18521fbd8f1ca6994b8f49f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c = s = -3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"149\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/9/8493c9ef9af23c69a3e22d0178d0a2c23794a70c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab + bc + ca = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f934ae7d192c44ea9528bb8c8edea92ca7f49eb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" />. Then\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/9/c19770805040b313fafffdedbfb2ee4726cf0414.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = -(a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = -(s-a)(s-b)(s-c) = -(-3-a)(-3-b)(-3-c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"644\" height=\"18\" /></center>\n<p>This is just the definition for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/c/fbc482e8944db939c317828bcbe1bb9e072bb745.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-P(-3) = \\boxed{023}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Alternatively, we can expand the expression to get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/1/d41a23c58ab7b5d1fe76c063b04b35cfc89d9fc2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} t &amp;= -(-3-a)(-3-b)(-3-c)\\\\  &amp;= (a+3)(b+3)(c+3)\\\\  &amp;= abc + 3[ab + bc + ca] + 9[a + b + c] + 27\\\\ t &amp;= 11 + 3(4) + 9(-3) + 27 = 23\\end{align*}\" width=\"344\" height=\"93\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution  2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution  2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Each term in the expansion of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/d/acd7907f1cfb9847e0b7a97c4914d38e959c11be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b)(b+c)(c+a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" /> has a total degree of 3.  Another way to get terms with degree 3 is to multiply out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/b/0fb0464d3c6aaa49e7c75ed1ebf9be6a9d1dd8f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b+c)(ab+bc+ca)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"191\" height=\"18\" />.  Expanding both of these expressions and comparing them shows that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/d/b8d7853e55671800d6492e42474e5058c618e148.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = (ab+bc+ca)(a+b+c)-abc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"424\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/b/adbeb3006b2a08d2e1bff8002f11fe7dd6ee20c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = -(a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = abc-(ab+bc+ca)(a+b+c) = 11-(4)(-3) = 23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"639\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\nA way to realize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/d/b8d7853e55671800d6492e42474e5058c618e148.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = (ab+bc+ca)(a+b+c)-abc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"424\" height=\"18\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e6513559d2c1ad6a9053ac1f71f6cb4f5503a712.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a + b)(b+c)(c+a) = a^2b + a^2c + b^2a + b^2c + c^2a + c^2b + abc + abc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"538\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>(Add an extra <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96a81938ca5e71faa6894d9d52ac776c9efbe75d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" />)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/3/bd34fa1167209c1e3cda451ec0efd415ac70488b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2b + a^2c + abc + b^2a + b^2c + abc + c^2a + c^2b + abc - abc =$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"468\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6ef26fc60b6295b94620bb4c28fc61994e7c12a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(ab + bc + ac) + b(ab + bc + ac) + c(ab + bc + ac) - abc =$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"466\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/1/e212407e796c87fd6978132ed4d60bcceb8d81dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a + b + c)(ab + bc + ac) - abc = (-3)(4) - 11 = -23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"424\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> is the negation of this, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/8/a8857857953747bb121ee289a649bd318c9ce86d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-(-23) = \\boxed{023}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"125\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~Extremelysupercooldude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/c/23c2dd73734af39c54bdbad0fb6aa24a98089685.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3+3x^2+4x-11=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"182\" height=\"16\" /> for roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f054be28a57624feee47965aad91fdc1b7a6792.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"16\" />\nIn the second cubic function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/9/a596b35f0eab2815c14f1435543253c92ea3184b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3+rx^2+sx+t=0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"177\" height=\"20\" /> the roots are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/a/37a53531b3f1d02a8b06fa5c73b31c7c3ea2ce03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b,b+c,c+a.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"137\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>By Vieta's formulae, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c27d44dd1ef2c33034499a5fe5cd35c5fd9abc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t= -(a+b)(b+c)(a+c).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"208\" height=\"18\" />\nAs we know that the sum of the roots of the first polynomial, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31b51deaa1a9e903d120a02141556c3e70e348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> by applying Vieta's again.\n</p><p>Using this fact, we can rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/4/fd4ed3d15679b7b5ffd018a4c7018d0fe02616c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-(-3-a)(-3-b)(-3-c) = (a+3)(b+3)(c+3).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"407\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Seeing this, we can find the value of the product of the roots by applying this to the first equation.\nThis can be done by setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/f/53f9eff3b41fdaff6c9cd30bb83495e9fee1936c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&#39;=a+3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"17\" /> so, from this, we see that we should plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/7/7c7e27bddf1474b894ef0066ba33028230e643f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&#39;-3$\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/c/23c2dd73734af39c54bdbad0fb6aa24a98089685.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3+3x^2+4x-11=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"182\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>After simplifying, we get that the polynomial is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/5/01577b760cfd3bbfdd424ee969920743221ed29e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&#39;^3 - 6x&#39;^2 + 13x&#39; - 23 = 0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"207\" height=\"16\" />\nGiven that the product of the roots of this equation is equivalent to our desired value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />, we can apply Vieta's formulae for a third time to find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/6/486d698273b99be511145cb56f1bad27fd5e0906.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = -(\\frac{-23}{1}) = \\boxed{023}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"161\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~MathWhiz35\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME\" title=\"1996 AIME\">1996 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1996 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1996\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017185731\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.040 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.062 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 304/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1766/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 88/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8481/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.020      1 -total\n 59.97%    7.808      1 Template:AIME_box\n 37.75%    4.915      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2988:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017185731 and revision id 290926. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}